%% Sequence 02b — Change task status
%% Updated: 2026-07-29.
%% Scenario: UpdateTaskStatusCommand owns one transition; DONE invokes a transaction-bound subordinate Command.
%% Evidence status: Implemented.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Project member / manager
    participant C as «boundary» UpdateTaskStatusController
    participant K as «control» UpdateTaskStatusCommand
    participant P as «domain» Task status policy
    participant D as «database» PostgreSQL
    participant X as «control» CompleteTaskAssignmentsCommand
    participant E as «outbound» TaskEventPublisher

    U->>C: PUT /tasks/:taskId/status
    C->>K: execute(UpdateTaskStatusDTO)
    activate K
    K->>D: BEGIN, lock task, load status + transitions
    D-->>K: task and workflow facts
    K->>P: validate permission, transition, submission
    P-->>K: allowed or policy violation
    alt Guard fails
        K->>D: ROLLBACK
        K-->>C: business error
    else Transition allowed
        K->>D: update task + Audit + staged notification
        opt category becomes DONE
            K->>X: execute(completion input, same transaction)
            X-->>K: assignments/review/outbox staged
        end
        K->>D: COMMIT
        K->>E: publish post-commit status event
        E-->>K: settled or isolated failure
        K-->>C: updated task detail
    end
    deactivate K
    C-->>U: task response or error
